Instruction: Read the segment of a merger agreement and answer the multiple-choice question by choosing the option that best characterizes the agreement.\nQuestion: When are representations and warranties required to be made according to the bring down provision?\nOption A: At Closing Only\nOption B: At Signing & At Closing\n\nMerger Agreement: Section 6.1 Conditions to Obligations of Acquirer and Merger Sub. The obligations of Acquirer and Merger Sub to effect the Merger are subject to the satisfaction or waiver by Acquirer at or prior to the Effective Time of the following conditions: (a) each of the representations and warranties of the Target contained in this Agreement shall be true and correct as of the date of this Agreement and as of the Closing Date, except for such failures to be true and correct as would not, individually or in the aggregate, have a Target Material Adverse Effect. (b) Notwithstanding the foregoing, representations and warranties that are qualified by materiality or Target Material Adverse Effect shall be deemed to be true and correct unless the failure to be so true and correct would reasonably be expected to have a Target Material Adverse Effect, in which case they need only be true and correct as of the Closing Date. (Page 42)\nAnswer:
