Instruction: Read the segment of a merger agreement and answer the multiple-choice question by choosing the option that best characterizes the agreement.\nQuestion: When are representations and warranties required to be made according to the bring down provision?\nOption A: At Closing Only\nOption B: At Signing & At Closing\n\nMerger Agreement: Section 9.4 Conditions to Obligations of Acquirer and Merger Sub to Effect the Merger. The obligations of Acquirer and Merger Sub to effect the Merger are, in addition to the conditions set forth in Section 9.3, further subject to the satisfaction or (to the extent not prohibited by Law) waiver by Acquirer at or prior to the Effective Time of the following conditions: (a) each of the representations and warranties of the Target contained in this Agreement, without giving effect to any materiality or "Target Material Adverse Effect" or similar qualifications therein, shall be true and correct as of the Closing Date, except for such failures to be true and correct as would not, individually or in the aggregate, have a Target Material Adverse Effect; provided, however, that any representations and warranties that are expressly made as of a specific date shall be so true and correct as of such specific date only. Additionally, (b) the representations and warranties in Section 3.1 and 3.5 shall be true and correct as of the date of this Agreement and as of the Closing Date as though made on and as of the Closing Date, except to the extent expressly made as of an earlier date, in which case as of such date. (Page 82)\nAnswer:
